<title>USA: CBOT Feb volume falls 11.4 pct yr/yr to 18.8 mln.</title>
<headline>CBOT Feb volume falls 11.4 pct yr/yr to 18.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade said the trading volume in its futures and options totalled 18,812,320 contracts in February, down 11.4 percent from 21,222,341 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for February 1997 and percentage change followed by February 1996 volume:</p>
<p>All futures     14,895,010     -12.3     16,991,566</p>
<p>  Agricultural   4,048,187     - 6.3	4,320,668</p>
<p>  Financial     10,842,466     -14.4     12,663,805</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   3,917,310     - 7.4	4,230,775</p>
<p>  Agricultural     982,131	+6.3	  923,959</p>
<p>  Financial	2,933,925     -11.3	3,306,094</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     7,522,816     -14.3	8,781,389</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 1,939,930     -16.1	2,313,071</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes  1,156,699     -11.8	1,311,967</p>
<p>  Wheat		373,411     -26.8	  510,138</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,482,968     -18.5	1,819,646</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 1,254,162     +11.2	1,128,280</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    481,841     + 8.8	  442,937</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     381,921     + 7.5	  355,220</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,287,446     + 2.4	2,233,416</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   455,275     -42.5	  791,482</p>
<p>  Corn		 406,762     - 3.3	  420,716</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   402,006     +30.2	  308,723</p>
<p>((DerivativesDesk(312)408-8750/E-mail:derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
